      'Confucius is the Latin form of Kong Fuzi, “Master Kong”. His given name was Kong Qiu, and he was born in 551 BC in or near the town of Zou, in the state of Lu, in what is now Shandong province. According to Sima Qian, his father, an older soldier, died when the boy was young, and the family lived in modest circumstances. Confucius later remarked that his poor origins had taught him many practical skills. He is said to have held minor posts, including work with granaries and livestock, before rising to office in Lu.',
