      'He regarded himself as a transmitter of the wisdom of earlier sages and not as an inventor of a new doctrine. His conversations with disciples, among them Yan Hui, Zilu, Zigong and Zengzi, were collected after his death in the Analects. Scholars note that the book was assembled over a long period and that some parts are later than others, so the “historical Confucius” is partly reconstructed from layers of tradition.',
